{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b7fc970c165ede96baa1e22adf6b32f4c1254148b3689fc7b942dd116c3f9acb","digest":{"component_or_area":"test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py upstream-URL assertion","key_entities":["_UPSTREAM_RE","test_notice_names_pandoc_its_version_and_its_licence","tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py","pandoc.org","github.com/jgm/pandoc","py/incomplete-url-substring-sanitization"],"problem_keywords":["incomplete URL substring sanitization","code-scanning alert","URL validation","host boundary"],"propositions":["Bare substring containment in upstream-URL assertion accepts lookalike hostnames (prefix and suffix styles) that do not actionably point at upstream.","The existing substring check `'pandoc.org' in text or 'github.com/jgm/pandoc' in text` allows false positives like https://notpandoc.org and https://pandoc.org.evil.com.","A scheme+host-anchored regex with negative lookahead end-of-host boundaries (`(?![\\w.-])` and `(?![\\w-])`) correctly rejects both lookalike classes while accepting legitimate NOTICE URLs.","The fix replaces the substring assertion with a compiled `_UPSTREAM_RE` pattern that enforces exact host and path boundaries, matching prior art from test_llm_fallback_chain.py without URL parsing machinery."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787688102308787001,"uuid":"a6cdce9f-2c24-405f-836b-1f16665f4f9e"}